{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q420287","formula":"Ca₆Al₂(SO₄)₃(OH)₁₂·26H₂O","hill":"Al2Ca6H64O50S3","elements":["H","O","Al","S","Ca"],"composition":{"H":64.0,"O":50.0,"S":3.0,"Al":2.0,"Ca":6.0},"names":{"en":"Ettringite","ru":"Эттрингит","uk":"Етрингіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ettringite is a hydrous calcium aluminium sulfate mineral with formula: Ca6Al2(SO4)3(OH)12·26H2O. It is a colorless to yellow mineral crystallizing in the trigonal system. The prismatic crystals are typically colorless, turning white on partial dehydration. It is part of the ettringite-group which includes other sulfates such as thaumasite and bentorite.","ru":"Эттринги́т — гидросульфоалюминат кальция, минерал с формулой Ca6Al2(SO4)3(OH)12·26H2O. Этот минерал с цветом от бесцветного до жёлтого кристаллизуется в тригональной системе. Призматические кристаллы обычно бесцветные, белеют в местах частичной дегидратации. Является частью группы эттрингита, которая включает и другие сульфаты, такие как таумасит и бенторит.","uk":"Етрингіт — рідкісний мінерал."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q420287","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ettringite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%AD%D1%82%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%95%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlesite-Ettringite-jmix07-166a.jpg","license"